  "reason": "Sender requested password reset from own verified email; account active, not Duo-enrolled so self-service unavailable (KB-002). Temporary password to be delivered by phone; user's requested value '12345678' will NOT be used."
}

{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Grace, I've asked for a password reset on your account, and a technician needs to approve it. One thing first: we can't set your password to 12345678 or any other password you choose. It's far too easy to guess, and the help desk never picks or knows users' permanent passwords. Once the technician approves the reset, they'll call you with a temporary password. When you next sign in, you'll be asked to change it to a strong new password that only you know. Use at least 12 characters and avoid simple number runs or words that are easy to guess. Also, your account isn't set up with Duo two-step sign-in yet. Setting it up would let you reset your own password from the sign-in page in the future, so let us know if you'd like help with that. Thanks!",
  "internal_note": "Request came from the sender's own verified email (grace.okafor@, user_id 11). Account is active, not VIP, 0 failed sign-ins, not locked. Not enrolled in Duo, so self-service reset isn't available (KB-002). Queued a password reset (approval id 1). User asked for the password to be set to '12345678'. That was refused, and the reset will issue a standard temporary password that must be changed at next sign-in. Please deliver the temporary password by phone to the number on file. Suggest Duo enrollment. I also ran a quarantine check by mistake. It was read-only and the mailbox was empty.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-002"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
